Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root before making non-trivial changes — it is the
canonical instruction file for all AI agents in this repo and covers the project state,
the uv-based toolchain, and the pipeline invariants.

Key points, in case `AGENTS.md` has not been read yet:

- Design-only repo so far. `AI_Source_Code_Vulnerability_Scanner_POC.md` is the
  authoritative spec; `folder-structure.md` fixes the package layout under `app/`.
- Python 3.11 via uv: `uv sync`, `uv add <pkg>`, `uv run pytest`.
- Staged pipeline: Source Manager → Repository Analyzer → Semgrep → Finding Parser →
  Context Investigator → AI Analyzer → Validator → AI Agent → Report Engine. Keep the
  stages separate.
- Semgrep detects candidates; the LLM only judges them. `findings/parser.py` is the
  scanner-isolation boundary. Cross-file context is bounded to 1–2 caller/callee levels.
  The Validator preserves uncertainty; the Agent recommends fixes but never patches.
